    "900(d) is an identity for all real x; 901(a/b/c) are genuinely inconsistent complete systems.",
    "902(a) retains distinct 5x-1 and 5x+1; correct roots are -4/5 and 0. It is not a second erratum.",
    "902(b/c/d) retain all back-substitution branches; 902(d) includes the repeated root -1.",
    "903 excludes negative squared-variable values, restores both signs for positive values, and keeps zero/repeated-root cases; raw Cyrillic к becomes natural Latin j.",
